WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.050
Wh-What was that sound?!

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:17.700
Oh, come on! Why is no one coming to save me?!

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.490
The dog, the monkey, the gorilla...

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:21.680
All of them, useless!

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.930
They'd better not have forgotten about me!

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:38.860
I've wasted enough time here.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:40.140
So...

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:43.930
I'd like you to hurry up and die now.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:45.270
Blow away!

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:06.960
You just don't give up, do you?

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:13.980
What the hell was that?

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:18.720
Can this really be happening? 
It's insane, damn it!

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:22.690
Honey-kun, don't you think 
you overdid it this time?

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:25.360
Hey, you're bleeding bad! Are you okay?

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:26.980
Shut your mouth.

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:35.740
You can't do something like this, can you?

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:39.990
Nothing to say, you coward?

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:05.470
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:15.210
<b>Move Forward!</b>

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:24.680
This isn't good. We're too incompatible.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:27.480
So I guess all we can do now is run, right?

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:28.420
No...

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:31.600
They'll probably chase us down
until they finish us off.

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:34.730
So what are we supposed to do, then?!

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.940
Uno-kun, have you worked out 
the layout of this place yet?

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:39.990
I'm starting to get it.

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:44.380
Then go straight ahead to the 
descending stairs with Jyugo-kun.

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:46.490
That's pretty far.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:49.750
We'll distract that guy as much as we can.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:50.750
Huh?

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:54.680
If you guys stick around, 
we might all get blown away.

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:57.950
But that'll mean... you guys will...

00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:59.510
Just do as I say.

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:01.510
If you don't, you two will die.

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:06.010
Move aside!

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.140
Another discussion?

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:17.900
Sorry, but I won't be giving you 
the time for that anymore.

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:22.570
Oh?

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:28.410
So you want to die first?

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:29.750
Get going!

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:32.160
Jyugo, let's go.

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:34.300
Okay.

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:35.540
What?

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:36.920
Over here!

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:38.630
Such insolence!

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:43.800
I told you, that won't work!

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.640
This isn't good...

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:01.170
Jeez...

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:03.520
My face didn't get scratched, did it?

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:06.760
You'd deserve it! All you
think about is showing off.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:11.080
I can't help that I'm so handsome. It's a curse.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:14.080
You should've just died earlier.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:17.310
Anyway, it's all going according to plan.

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:19.220
They've both gone on ahead of us.

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:23.820
Better believe it. Having that 
good-for-nothing around was killing us.

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:25.840
You're being mean again.

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:28.420
I hope they can make it.

00:05:28.420 --> 00:05:30.740
That guy seems persistent.

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:32.400
If I was gonna get chased,

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:33.970
I'd want Kaguya-chan to chase me.

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:36.730
Let's just humor him for a while.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:39.550
We can run after that.

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:48.040
What's wrong, Jyugo?

00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:55.780
Let's go.

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:01.960
You think something like 
that is gonna work?!

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:10.720
Don't mock me!

00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:12.350
No good, huh...

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:17.850
I'll explain to Kiji in detail 
about how you guys died!

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:19.480
Got a plan?

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:20.860
You?

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:22.480
If I did, I wouldn't ask!

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:46.510
N-No, this can't be...

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:55.910
Why?

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:03.520
You... What is that form?

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:07.560
<i>Is this the guy he was talking about?</i>

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:12.910
I'll finish off that monster myself.

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:16.030
<i>What he meant by those words...</i>

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:19.860
<i>Finally... I finally...</i>

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:22.170
Enki-san...

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:27.920
I'm prepared to go to the 
ends of the earth with you.

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:31.800
And I don't mean to pry, but...

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:35.930
I am a bit curious about 
what you're thinking.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:38.180
What are you planning to do?

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:48.960
It's something you wouldn't understand.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:52.500
I see...

00:07:53.930 --> 00:07:55.610
<i>I understand now.</i>

00:07:57.420 --> 00:08:00.420
I will kill you.

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:02.330
If I kill you...

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:06.250
<i>Then, Enki-san, I can understand you.</i>

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:13.640
<i>He cut Bashosen's wind?</i>

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:17.220
Impossible!

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:20.970
There's no way he can do that 
just by swinging a blade.

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:49.380
Uh... This is, um...

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:51.480
Huh?

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:53.440
Is this like a concealed weapon?

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:55.360
How is it made?

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:57.300
It looks like a special type of metal.

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:59.400
What is it made of?

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:01.380
If you can swing it with one arm,

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:04.300
I assume it's relatively light.

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:05.920
Special alloys?

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:08.090
No, is it carbon steel?

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:09.610
Or could it be...

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:11.230
Huh?

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:13.440
But swords are made out of metal.

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:16.070
Maybe it has a different carbon level?

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:17.740
It looks more like stainless...

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:21.990
No one is normal around here, huh?

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:25.620
Do you think you've won?

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:30.750
You think that was the 
true power of Bashosen?

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:34.760
Don't get cocky just because 
you sliced through a little wind.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:39.430
I will never lose to a monster like you!

00:09:50.990 --> 00:09:54.600
What's wrong? Why don't you try 
cutting it like you did last time?

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:59.960
You're not even worth his time!

00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:02.370
I'll finish you off myself!

00:10:11.490 --> 00:10:13.620
You're no big deal at all.

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:20.090
What?!

00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:27.350
He took my wind... into the blade?!

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:38.240
<i>This can't be! How did 
the wind get stronger?!</i>

00:10:40.850 --> 00:10:42.700
<i>Who the heck is he?!</i>

00:10:54.140 --> 00:10:55.850
Jyugo! Hold on, I'm—

00:10:55.850 --> 00:10:56.980
He's fine.

00:10:56.980 --> 00:10:57.760
Huh?

00:11:02.460 --> 00:11:03.660
He...

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:06.050
So, why did you guys come back?

00:11:06.050 --> 00:11:08.020
It wasn't me. It was Jyugo.

00:11:08.020 --> 00:11:09.510
Jyugo-kun?

00:11:10.090 --> 00:11:12.270
He hates losing more than you'd think.

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:15.630
He's kinda like your partner, really.

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:25.630
Jeez, this is the second time.

00:11:25.630 --> 00:11:27.250
Enough already.

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:29.410
Huh? What?

00:11:30.340 --> 00:11:33.920
You can't do something like that, can you?

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:36.920
No one can drown like you do.

00:11:42.670 --> 00:11:43.480
Huh?

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:49.930
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:54.940
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:04.960
Hakkai.

00:12:04.960 --> 00:12:05.950
Yes?

00:12:06.190 --> 00:12:08.970
I sense multiple presences.

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:12.210
Did you truly capture them?

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:13.780
Yes, I did.

00:12:13.780 --> 00:12:16.710
But I left everything to Gojyou after that.

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:19.690
He seemed very motivated

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:22.950
and eagerly volunteered to manage 
underground level two,

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:26.270
so there's no way he'll fail, I'm sure.

00:12:26.270 --> 00:12:31.480
And even if he does,
he'll settle it in his own way.

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:34.410
But there's more, isn't there?

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:36.480
To the presence you've felt.

00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:39.510
The other is not a presence.

00:12:39.510 --> 00:12:41.430
It's something else.

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:42.430
Something else?

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:44.440
Something not human.

00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:48.240
You can't kill something that's not human 
the way humans kill each other.

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:50.740
Are you saying you can kill it?

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:56.500
If so, that means you're not human.

00:13:04.750 --> 00:13:06.170
That sound...

00:13:06.170 --> 00:13:07.890
It's Gojyou's Bashosen.

00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:10.730
I felt his presence, a little.

00:13:10.730 --> 00:13:12.030
But it's odd...

00:13:12.030 --> 00:13:12.900
What is?

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:13.600
Well...

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:14.520
What?

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:17.200
There's a presence other than Gojyou's.

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:19.650
Like, something different...

00:13:19.990 --> 00:13:23.270
So?! What is this "something"?!

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:26.790
I can't explain it with you rushing me!

00:13:26.790 --> 00:13:28.370
I said it's something, so it's something!

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:29.160
Take the hint!

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:30.140
Take the hint?!

00:13:30.140 --> 00:13:31.570
Don't be a pain in the ass!

00:13:31.570 --> 00:13:33.410
Are you my girlfriend,
trying to cheer me up?

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:34.490
Like hell!

00:13:36.180 --> 00:13:37.790
<i>So annoying.</i>

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:46.930
What are you guys doing here?

00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:48.430
<i>They're...</i>

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:50.160
I've never seen you before.

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:51.180
Where are you from?

00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:52.390
Huh?

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:55.920
They no longer have the charms.
Does this mean they're back to normal?

00:13:55.920 --> 00:13:57.560
Y-You think?

00:13:58.150 --> 00:13:59.600
Well...

00:13:59.600 --> 00:14:01.940
Before we knew it, 
we were locked up in here.

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:05.090
We've got this problem, so we're 
out of the cell at the moment,

00:14:05.090 --> 00:14:06.700
but it's a good thing we ran into you guys.

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:10.940
Our supervising officer should 
be here, and we're looking...

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:15.350
Uno?!

00:14:15.350 --> 00:14:20.520
Sorry, but we can't allow inmates to 
escape, no matter what the reason.

00:14:20.520 --> 00:14:22.590
Come with us quietly.

00:14:22.990 --> 00:14:24.200
Uno?

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:27.090
Why'd you have to do that?! At least listen!

00:14:27.320 --> 00:14:30.300
Huh? Why should we listen to you?

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:32.970
It's obvious you guys have escaped.

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:35.600
Fine. I'll tell you the truth.

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:36.850
The truth?

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:42.410
Your former supervisor has escaped and 
locked us up, along with the guards.

00:14:42.410 --> 00:14:44.600
I don't know what he's planning,

00:14:44.600 --> 00:14:48.110
but right now, I think that's more 
important than us. Don't you agree?

00:14:48.440 --> 00:14:52.210
Besides, a guard from your building 
just tried to kill us, and—

00:14:52.210 --> 00:14:56.740
Huh? You expect us to believe 
the ramblings of an inmate?

00:14:56.740 --> 00:15:00.620
And to bring up Enki-san of all things...

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:02.830
You've got some nerve.

00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:04.990
If that's the case,

00:15:04.990 --> 00:15:09.260
how do you explain us being inside the
underground prison, which isn't used anymore?

00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:13.070
What inmate would enter the 
underground prison willingly?

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:15.510
You're right. That is strange.

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:19.640
But so what? It doesn't change 
the fact that you're inmates.

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:23.410
We can't allow you punks to wander 
around underground any longer.

00:15:23.410 --> 00:15:26.250
And not only are you here, 
but you know about Enki-san.

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:27.750
That's suspicious.

00:15:27.750 --> 00:15:31.040
We can't have you causing any 
more trouble in this building.

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:32.210
Depending on your actions,

00:15:32.210 --> 00:15:34.530
we will show no mercy, in accordance 
with the rules of Building 5.

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:37.060
Hey, no one told me any of this.

00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:39.440
They're gonna try to catch us either way.

00:15:39.440 --> 00:15:42.420
Oh, jeez. This is why I hate meatheads.

00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:46.730
What the hell was that?!

00:15:46.730 --> 00:15:49.640
Oh, my apologies. My hand slipped.

00:15:49.640 --> 00:15:51.550
Trois, what are you...

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:53.590
It's no use talking to these guys.

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:56.550
You guys know what to do! Get going!

00:15:58.680 --> 00:15:59.680
You're not getting away!

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:09.530
Oh, my apologies. It seems 
you accidentally got caught.

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:12.410
Jyugo, now's our chance!

00:16:12.410 --> 00:16:13.660
I know!

00:16:20.410 --> 00:16:21.740
You're not going anywhere.

00:16:21.740 --> 00:16:25.330
I won't let you go any further!

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:27.460
He's seriously persistent...

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:28.000
Uno!

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:29.840
Don't come near me!

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:31.340
Just go!

00:16:31.560 --> 00:16:32.590
I can't!

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:37.640
Get real, you idiot!

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:41.220
If you stop here, how would they all feel?!

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:51.790
Jyugo-kun lost again!

00:16:51.790 --> 00:16:53.740
Why do you suck so bad?

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:57.710
You really can't do anything 
besides jailbreaking, can you?

00:16:57.710 --> 00:16:58.370
Hmph...

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:02.120
But it's pretty cool to have 
something only you can do.

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:05.620
It's special to be able to 
escape that much! Right?

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:07.130
I guess so.

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:16.680
Just go already!

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:19.010
Go do something only you can do!

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:25.630
Move... Move forward!

00:17:33.220 --> 00:17:35.280
<i>Hurry up and bring him back.</i>

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:37.160
<i>It's easy for you, right?</i>

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:39.660
<i>Go and give him a hard time like always...</i>

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:41.960
<i>That damn gorilla!</i>

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:43.540
I'm coming!

00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:48.920
Whoa!

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:50.740
Stop showing off!

00:17:50.740 --> 00:17:51.940
Ow...

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:54.180
I can't breathe! Ow!

00:17:56.140 --> 00:17:56.930
Trois!

00:17:58.570 --> 00:18:00.900
Ow! It hurts!

00:18:00.900 --> 00:18:02.560
It seriously hurts! Ow!

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:04.510
Don't worry, it'll be over soon.

00:18:04.510 --> 00:18:05.430
You're lying!

00:18:05.760 --> 00:18:08.480
That's what doctors say!

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:11.940
You again!

00:18:13.140 --> 00:18:15.190
Shit, this is a repeat of last time!

00:18:17.600 --> 00:18:19.640
Wh-What's Ruka-san doing here?

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:20.950
Wh-What's going on?

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:23.510
That's what we've been telling you guys!

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:25.620
This guy is attacking us!

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:26.830
Hurry up and save us!

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:28.080
Or capture him!

00:18:28.530 --> 00:18:31.400
This is... a dilemma.

00:18:31.400 --> 00:18:33.780
If what they're saying is true,

00:18:33.780 --> 00:18:35.890
then that thing about Enki-san escaping is...

00:18:35.890 --> 00:18:38.870
If people find out, it'll mean 
more than just a pay cut!

00:18:38.870 --> 00:18:41.850
Jailbreaking is bad, so... But...

00:18:42.340 --> 00:18:47.350
What? You two are planning 
to disobey me? Huh?

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:50.830
Wh-What should we do, Youriki?

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:53.010
What should we prioritize?

00:18:53.010 --> 00:18:56.230
Ruka-san is our predecessor, and those 
guys are inmates from another building.

00:18:56.520 --> 00:19:00.160
Hmm... They're all inmates 
and have escaped.

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:02.210
This is very difficult.

00:19:02.210 --> 00:19:05.200
Which should we capture first? Hmm...

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:06.710
Agh! You meatheads!

00:19:06.710 --> 00:19:08.390
Think really hard!

00:19:08.390 --> 00:19:12.130
At least show enough spirit to capture 
all of us in the worst case, you dummy!

00:19:13.300 --> 00:19:14.760
All right, I've decided!

00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:17.780
Let's handle all the outsiders first!

00:19:17.780 --> 00:19:21.190
Agreed. We can think more 
about it afterwards.

00:19:21.190 --> 00:19:23.390
Argh! You idiots!

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:25.160
What now?

00:19:25.160 --> 00:19:27.640
Are we gonna end up getting 
captured by them anyway?

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:48.160
If we attack, it'll be considered 
obstruction of official duties.

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:50.200
I say we have a huge disadvantage.

00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:54.680
Getting caught by those numbskulls and
getting our sentences extended is no joke.

00:19:54.680 --> 00:19:56.960
Aw, jeez! I hate idiots!

00:19:57.320 --> 00:20:01.590
Well, it's not like there isn't 
a way to get out of here.

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:02.590
Seriously?!

00:20:02.870 --> 00:20:04.350
And this is just a guess,

00:20:04.350 --> 00:20:06.350
but I think Kiji-san is on this floor.

00:20:06.590 --> 00:20:07.850
Seriously?!

00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:26.880
Get out of the way!

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:30.060
Kiji is here?!

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:32.050
Why are you telling us this now?!

00:20:32.050 --> 00:20:36.020
Well, with all the wind blowing 
and the smell of gunpowder,

00:20:36.020 --> 00:20:37.540
I didn't notice it right away.

00:20:37.790 --> 00:20:39.800
But now it's very clear.

00:20:40.060 --> 00:20:41.890
The smell of Kiji-san's perfume.

00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:42.800
Perfume...

00:20:43.580 --> 00:20:44.820
Now that you mention it,

00:20:44.820 --> 00:20:46.520
I'm suddenly starting to smell it, too.

00:20:46.520 --> 00:20:48.320
It's mixing with all the other smells.

00:20:48.320 --> 00:20:49.680
It's disgusting!

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:53.930
But I guess the strong scent 
means he's close by.

00:20:53.930 --> 00:20:55.940
When I got closer to Ruka earlier,

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:57.790
I detected Kiji-san's scent.

00:20:57.790 --> 00:21:01.190
So I thought, maybe he was with 
Kiji-san not too long ago.

00:21:01.590 --> 00:21:05.060
It's not for certain, but what do you think?

00:21:05.060 --> 00:21:07.070
Okay, lend me your ears.

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:12.330
Huh?!

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:13.060
Well?

00:21:13.060 --> 00:21:15.260
There's no way that's gonna work!

00:21:15.260 --> 00:21:17.080
It's leaving too much to chance!

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:20.310
You think so? I think we should go for it.

00:21:20.310 --> 00:21:23.090
Longshot odds get the 
adrenaline pumping, right?

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:27.060
Oh? Or could it be that Honey-chan 
isn't feeling confident?

00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:28.220
What did you say?!

00:21:30.220 --> 00:21:32.470
So annoying... I'll do it!

00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:35.350
We will definitely win!

00:21:35.900 --> 00:21:39.610
I'm betting on it, so there's 
no way we're gonna lose.

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:25.630 --> 00:23:28.420
With everyone's help, I was 
able to get past the enemy,

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:31.840
and finally reach the underground 
prison where Hajime is held.

00:23:31.840 --> 00:23:34.550
There, I see a demon.

00:23:35.110 --> 00:23:37.070
Next episode: "Sarabaka."

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Sarabaka</b>

00:23:37.070 --> 00:23:39.930
I'm coming for you, Enki Gokuu!
